<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cotys I (Odrysian)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. 384–360 BCE</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Cotys I was king of the Odrysian kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thrace">Thrace</a> from 384 to 360 BCE. He strengthened royal power over the Thracian tribes and fought <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/athens">Athens</a> for control of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gallipoli">Thracian Chersonese</a>, although he had married his daughter to the Athenian general <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iphicrates">Iphicrates</a>. He was murdered in 360 BCE, after which his kingdom was divided among rival heirs, opening Thrace to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philip-ii-of-macedon">Philip II of Macedon</a>.</p></div>
